Reused evidence
- None.

New evidence
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Deutschland 2022","publisher":"Amnesty International Deutschland","publication_date":"2023-03-28","url":"https://www.amnesty.de/informieren/amnesty-report/deutschland-2022","claim":"Amnesty said unzureichende Ermittlungen bei Vorwürfen über diskriminierende Personenkontrollen and the lack of an independent complaint mechanism continued to block justice for police abuse complaints in Germany.","locator":"Berichtszeitraum 1. Januar 2022 bis 31. Dezember 2022; section on 'Recht auf Gerechtigkeit, Wahrheit und Wiedergutmachung'","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Major rights-organization country report covering the full target year; specific findings are explicit and well-sourced.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers 2022 and names the relevant police-accountability gap.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect ruler attribution only; this is a national institutional condition under Scholz's government, not a personal order.","contrary_evidence":["Germany remained an open reporting environment rather than a closed repressive system.","The report criticizes investigation quality, not a pattern of systematic state terror."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.4"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Deutschland 2022","publisher":"Amnesty International Deutschland","publication_date":"2023-03-28","url":"https://www.amnesty.de/informieren/amnesty-report/deutschland-2022","claim":"Amnesty said some protests were disproportionately restricted and that a court held permanent protest camps protected by the freedom of assembly.","locator":"Berichtszeitraum 1. Januar 2022 bis 31. Dezember 2022; section on 'Recht auf Versammlungsfreiheit'","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Same annual report, but this is a distinct claim on protest rights and restrictions with direct 2022 relevance.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers 2022 protest treatment.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect attribution to the federal political environment under Scholz; protest control was mostly exercised by Länder and local authorities.","contrary_evidence":["The same report also notes a court-protected protest-camp precedent, so the picture is mixed rather than uniformly repressive.","The restrictions discussed are not evidence of nationwide political terror."],"lenses":["3B.8","3B.9"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Deutschland 2022","publisher":"Amnesty International Deutschland","publication_date":"2023-03-28","url":"https://www.amnesty.de/informieren/amnesty-report/deutschland-2022","claim":"Amnesty reported that in August 2022 a 16-year-old Senegalese refugee was killed by several shots from a machine gun during a disproportionate police operation, with criminal investigations still ongoing at year-end.","locator":"Berichtszeitraum 1. Januar 2022 bis 31. Dezember 2022; section on discrimination / police action","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific, contemporaneous, and materially important incident documented by a leading rights NGO.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 incident and after-effects.","ruler_attribution":"Weak-to-indirect national attribution: a police killing under a Scholz-era government, but operational control was regional and incident-specific.","contrary_evidence":["The report describes an isolated severe incident, not a generalized national terror policy.","Investigations were still ongoing, so final legal responsibility was unsettled at year-end."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.7","3B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"BASU c. ALLEMAGNE","publisher":"European Court of Human Rights","publication_date":"2022-10-18","url":"https://hudoc.echr.coe.int/fre?i=001-220369","claim":"The Court held that Germany failed to secure an effective independent investigation into an arguable racial-profiling complaint arising from a police identity check, violating Article 14 in conjunction with Article 8.","locator":"Judgment summary, introduction and key holding","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative judicial finding from the ECHR on a German policing and discrimination case.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 judgment, directly relevant to the year's accountability environment.","ruler_attribution":"Institutional attribution, not personal; it reflects state-level investigative failure under Scholz's chancellorship.","contrary_evidence":["The case concerns a 2012 stop and the adequacy of later review, not a 2022 order by Scholz.","It shows a remedy failure more than direct policy abuse."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.4"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Versammlungsrechtlicher Schutz eines Protestcamps und seiner infrastrukturellen Einrichtungen","publisher":"Bundesverwaltungsgericht","publication_date":"2022-05-24","url":"https://www.bverwg.de/240522U6C9.20.0","claim":"The Federal Administrative Court held that a protest camp can generally count as a protected assembly under Article 8 GG and that its necessary infrastructure can also fall under assembly protection.","locator":"Leitsätze 1-3","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Binding domestic court decision on protest rights and their protection scope.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 ruling.","ruler_attribution":"Indicates the legal environment under Scholz's government, not a personal directive by Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["The case also confirms that authorities may still limit duration in some circumstances.","This is a legal-protection source, not evidence of executive restraint by itself."],"lenses":["3B.8"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundeskabinett - Ergebnisse","publisher":"Bundesregierung","publication_date":"2022-12-14","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/aktuelles/bundeskabinett-ergebnisse-2153466","claim":"The cabinet adopted a draft law to strengthen measures for democratic participation, diversity, extremism prevention, and political education.","locator":"TOP-1-Liste / agenda items for the 44th cabinet meeting on 14 December 2022","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official cabinet decision published on the federal government site, contemporaneous with the target year.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 executive action.","ruler_attribution":"Cabinet-level action under Scholz; precise implementation and downstream effect remain broader than Scholz alone.","contrary_evidence":["This is a draft-law decision, not proof of immediate harm reduction.","The measure is preventive and institutional, so its effect is indirect."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.5","3B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Rede von Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz zu 25 Jahren Freundeskreis Yad Vashem in Deutschland","publisher":"Bundesregierung","publication_date":"2022-09-05","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/service/newsletter-und-abos/bulletin/rede-von-bundeskanzler-olaf-scholz-2122952","claim":"Scholz said the Nazis had begun their murderous intent by trying to erase Jewish life and used the speech to reaffirm Germany's historical responsibility toward Jewish life and remembrance.","locator":"Opening paragraphs of the speech","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct Scholz speech in the federal bulletin archive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 speech, useful for public stance and vulnerable-group protection context.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz rhetoric; it is a public statement, not an operational security order.","contrary_evidence":["Rhetoric is not the same as enforcement or complaint-handling reform.","The speech is symbolic and commemorative, not a concrete anti-violence program."],"lenses":["3B.3","3B.7","3B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Couverture de base pour les réfugiés ukrainiens","publisher":"Gouvernement fédéral","publication_date":"2022-04-27","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-fr/service/archives/couverture-de-base-ukrainiens-2028896","claim":"The federal government decided that from 1 June 2022 Ukrainian refugees could access basic social-security benefits, healthcare coverage, integration courses, and job-center support, with Germany4Ukraine as a central information portal.","locator":"Archival article dated 27 April 2022; sections 'Aides provenant d'une source unique' and support details","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous government decision and implementation summary with concrete benefits and dates.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 refugee-protection policy.","ruler_attribution":"Cabinet-level attribution under Scholz; this is executive policy in the target year.","contrary_evidence":["This is protection and integration policy, not direct evidence on policing or political violence.","The policy concerns refugees from Ukraine, so it is a targeted vulnerable-group measure rather than a universal domestic-safety fix."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.10"]}

Search and rejection summary
- I reviewed roughly 25-40 documents across federal archives, the Bundestag, the ECtHR, the Bundesverwaltungsgericht, BKA/BMI material, and independent rights reporting.
- Kept the strongest 2022-relevant items that actually move 3B: police-accountability failures, protest-rights protection, one serious police-violence incident, anti-extremism cabinet action, Jewish-life protection rhetoric, and refugee protection.
- Rejected many broad crime, extremism, and statistics pages because they were either too generic, only partially 2022-specific, or mostly descriptive context rather than ruler-relevant evidence.
- Rejected several post-2022 documents when they repeated the same baseline without adding target-year detail.
- Rejected international-war and Ukraine-support material that belonged more properly in 2B unless it had a direct domestic safety consequence; I only retained the refugee-protection item because it directly affected domestic protection for civilians in Germany.
- Rejected local or state-level policing stories when they did not clearly add national-ruler attribution beyond what the national rights and court record already showed.

Remaining gaps
- The record supports a mixed but low-severity domestic-safety picture: open constitutional protections, meaningful protest rights, serious but isolated police/accountability failures, and active anti-extremism measures.
- I did not find a clean 2022 federal mechanism that solved the independent-police-investigation gap; that remains a real weakness in the record.
- There is limited evidence of Scholz personally directing domestic security policy on a day-to-day basis; most of the material is cabinet-level or institutional.
- More search would help if you want deeper coverage on police oversight reforms, regional protest-policing episodes, or 2022 hate-crime implementation, but it is not likely to change the overall evidentiary shape much.
